From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 19:59:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Haswell NRI: Do not truncate write leveling global offset

calc_global_offset() returns the PI offset needed when the write delay
target is outside the SC_WR_ADD_DELAY range: +128 or more for targets
above 2, and -128 or less for targets below 0. get_pi_offset() takes
this value as int8_t, so +128 becomes -128 and +/-256 becomes 0.

The write leveling clean-up hits this when the bytes of a rank only
pass with a write delay offset of 3, or when refining the target moves
it to 3 or more, or to -2 or less. The bytes then end up 256 PI ticks
(two SC_WR_ADD_DELAY steps) away from where they passed, which is
likely to make later write training fail. The code before the clean-up
used int16_t for this offset.

Take the global offset as int16_t again.

Fixes: commit f86a9eb0e153 ("Haswell NRI: Tidy up write leveling clean-up routine")

TEST=Built for lenovo/w541 with native raminit. Not tested on
hardware yet.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 .../intel/haswell/native_raminit/train_jedec_write_leveling.c   | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/train_jedec_write_leveling.c b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/train_jedec_write_leveling.c
index a8ce54053..d502cfa39 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/train_jedec_write_leveling.c
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/train_jedec_write_leveling.c
@@ -56,7 +56,7 @@ static int16_t calc_global_offset(const int8_t tgt_off)
 		return 0;
 }
 
-static int16_t get_pi_offset(const int8_t b_off, const int8_t tgt_off, const int8_t g_off)
+static int16_t get_pi_offset(const int8_t b_off, const int8_t tgt_off, const int16_t g_off)
 {
 	return (b_off - tgt_off) * 128 + g_off;
 }
